            <ArticleTitle>Modelling binary data from a three-period cross-over trial.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>555-64</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A new method of analysing binary data from a three-treatment, three-period cross-over trial is described. This method is based on a log-linear model and mirrors the analysis of continuous data. It is an extension of the method we introduced recently for the analysis of binary data from a two-treatment, two-period cross-over trial. We illustrate our method using data from a trial which compared two analgesics and a placebo for the relief of primary dysmenorrhea.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
